  "summary": "I added a \"Tour\" button below the canvas, in normal page flow, outside the 640x360 overlay. It passes typecheck, but I haven't run it in a browser, so the tour timing is untested. Clicking it focuses each planet from Mercury outward for 3 seconds per planet, with the info panel showing and the usual eased camera move. After Uranus it returns to the overview. While touring the button reads \"Stop tour\", and clicking it ends the tour and returns to the overview. A manual planet click, a click on empty space, Escape, `__focusPlanet` or `__unfocus` also ends the tour. `window.__TASK_STATE__` now has a read-only `touring` boolean."
